# 6) Kullanıcı hikayeleri (örnek, backlog başlangıcı)

* As a customer I want to create a ticket with photos so that I can request service.
* As a technician I want to see nearby tickets so I can accept jobs close to me.
* As an admin I want to assign a ticket manually so that urgent jobs are handled.
  (…) — Her birini sprintlere böl.

---

# 7) Acceptance Criteria örnekleri (kalite garantisi)

* Ticket oluşturma: “Given user fills form and uploads at least 1 photo, When submit, Then ticket is stored in DB with status=created and a confirmation email is sent.”
* Teknisyen üstlenme: “When technician hits ‘accept’, Then ticket.assigned_to = technician_id AND status = assigned AND customer receives notification.”

---

# 8) Ölçümler & KPI (neye bakılmalı)

* İlk yanıt süresi (time to first assign)
* Ortalama çözüm süresi
* İlk ziyaret çözüm oranı
* Tekrar şikayet oranı
* SLA ihlali oranı
* NPS / CSAT skorları

---

# 9) Teknik entegrasyon dokümanı — başlangıç (ERP/CRM-ready)

**Data modeller (zorunlu alanlar, örnek):**

* Customer: id, external_id, name, phone, email, address, metadata
* Ticket: id, external_id, customer_id, product_category, product_brand, summary, description, priority, status, created_at, updated_at, sla_deadline
* Technician: id, external_id, name, skills[], certifications[], location, status
* Invoice: id, ticket_id, amount, status, external_reference

**API design (örnek):**

* `POST /api/v1/tickets` — create
* `GET /api/v1/tickets/{id}` — get
* `POST /api/v1/webhook` — receive webhook (with HMAC)
* Events: `ticket.created`, `ticket.updated`, `ticket.closed`, `invoice.created`

**Webhook contract:**

```json
{
  "version": "1.0",
  "event": "ticket.created",
  "timestamp": "2025-12-02T09:00:00Z",
  "payload": { ... }
}
```

**Auth:** HMAC signature header veya OAuth2 client credentials.

